109:      - `triggerHook(event, payload, ctx)`: invokes registered hook handlers in order.
110:      - `executeCommand(name, args, ctx)`: invokes registered command handler.
111:      - `getArgumentCompletions(name, prefix)`: evaluates argument completions.
112: 3. **`createMockRedactor(options)`**:
113:    - Spies: `isEnabledSpy`, `getConfigSpy`, `redactSpy`, `setEnabledSpy`, `getRulesSpy`.
114:    - Allows unit tests to run deterministically in < 1ms without initializing the native machine learning model weights of `@desert-ant-labs/redact/native`.
115: 
116: ### 2.3 Verification of Zero Naming or Import Collisions
117: 
118: | Collision Vector | Risk Identified | Architectural Resolution |
119: |---|---|---|
120: | **Vitest File Matching** | Shared helper file being mistakenly run as an empty test suite | Name helper `tests/mock-pi.ts` (without `.test.ts` suffix). Vitest ignores non-test files |
121: | **ESM Module Resolution** | NodeNext module resolution error TS2691 | All relative imports specify `.js` (e.g. `import { createMockExtensionAPI } from "./mock-pi.js"`) |
122: | **Missing Type Exports** | Error TS2305 on `AutocompleteItem` | Never import `AutocompleteItem` from `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`. Use `{ value: string; label: string }` |
123: | **Test Suite Names** | Colliding Vitest reporter output | Distinct scoped descriptions: `describe("Extension Hooks (src/hooks/index.ts)", ...)` and `describe("Extension Commands (src/commands/pii.ts)", ...)` |
124: | **State Bleed** | Mutated redactor state between tests | Instantiate fresh mocks and redactor instances in `beforeEach()` blocks |
125: | **TypeScript Typecheck** | Build failure during `npm run typecheck` | `tsconfig.json` maintains `"include": ["src/**/*"]`. The mock harness and both test suites are 100% type-valid under `tsc --strict` |
126: 
